[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2625074768","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102160#issuecomment-2625074768","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102160","id":2625074768,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cd3ZQ","user":{"login":"huwpascoe","id":1812087,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MTIwODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1812087?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe","html_url":"https://github.com/huwpascoe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T17:05:35Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T17:05:35Z","body":"Here's the problem:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/ee4acfbfbf15b3528c34a8d4f65d66097e636044/scene/2d/light_occluder_2d.cpp#L183-L201\n\nIn editor mode it draws the occluder with an arbitrary black + 60% alpha. The clockwise cull shows how this editor shape looks as-is.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2625074768/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2625305391","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102160#issuecomment-2625305391","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102160","id":2625305391,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cevsv","user":{"login":"cashew-olddew","id":155181921,"node_id":"U_kgDOCT_jYQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155181921?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew","html_url":"https://github.com/cashew-olddew","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cashew-olddew/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T18:47:37Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T18:47:37Z","body":"I think there might still be some misunderstanding in regards to the issue. The problem was not necessarily that the occluder was darkening the sprite in the editor, but rather that, no matter where it was placed relative to the sprite, it did not do what the documentation says:\n\n> LightOccluder2Ds follows the usual 2D drawing order. This is important for 2D lighting, as **this is how you control whether the occluder should occlude the sprite itself or not**.\n\nLet's look at the \"Occluder Above\" example:\n- The occluder is above the sprite in the scene tree, thus, it should draw behind it\n- As per the docs, when I run the game, I expect to see a sprite casting a shadow, with the sprite being fully lit (similarly to how the clockwise occluder example works)\n- Instead, the sprite is occluded as well\n\nSo, if I place a sprite and an occluder on top of each other, to me, two cases seem plausible:\n- **the docs are wrong:** the sprite will always be occluded, no matter where the occluder is relative to it in the scene\n- **the docs are right:** which means that there's an issue with this feature in the engine","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2625305391/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2626606884","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102160#issuecomment-2626606884","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102160","id":2626606884,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cjtck","user":{"login":"huwpascoe","id":1812087,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MTIwODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1812087?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe","html_url":"https://github.com/huwpascoe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/huwpascoe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T08:20:42Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T08:20:42Z","body":"@clayjohn is there a definitive answer? Are occluders supposed to respect z-index?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2626606884/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2627867566","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102160#issuecomment-2627867566","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102160","id":2627867566,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cohOu","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T17:30:24Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T17:30:24Z","body":"> [@clayjohn](https://github.com/clayjohn) is there a definitive answer? Are occluders supposed to respect z-index?\n\nI don't think they do. CCing @Calinou Who added that section of the docs in https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/pull/6424","author_association":"MEMBER","